    "researcher_notes": "HAS_REF re-verify of long narrative. Current ref bundled aramco.com (unreachable by verifier — Aramco bot-blocks) with Wikipedia, Britannica, Saudipedia (all live). The narrative's claims are spread across the working sources: route Qaisumah→Jordan/Syria/Golan→Sidon, Aramco construction, 30/31-inch pipe, ~1,213-1,214 km, capacity progression to ~500,000 bpd, 1976 cross-border cessation, intermittent Saudi/Jordan ops to 1983/1990, Dec-2020 first Saudi industrial-heritage-site designation. Wikipedia covers route/diameter/length/capacity/dates; Britannica covers route/diameter/dates; Saudipedia covers Saudi-Aramco ownership, Abqaiq processing, Qaisumah, Sidon/Lebanon, 1950 inauguration, 1975 war disruption, 1983/1990, and the 2020 heritage designation ('First industrial heritage site in the Kingdom ... selected in 2020'). Dropped the dead Aramco link; replacement set = Wikipedia + Britannica + Saudipedia. Note: the '2001 de-cruding' detail in the GEM narrative is NOT verifiable on the working sources (it traces to the blocked Aramco elements article) — flagged as single-source/unverified, not overwritten. 3 independent working origins → high for the bulk of the narrative."
